       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Higher doses don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect. They do add a substantial risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't see a clinical scenario where this regimen would help the patient, so I can't enter it as written.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the highest standard regimen. I can add a note with your rationale.\n- **Add other pain or inflammation control.** If the goal is stronger effect, I can enter ibuprofen at a standard dose along with a scheduled adjunct such as acetaminophen. I can also enter another agent you choose.\n- **Review with pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs a dose outside labeled limits, a pharmacist or clinical pharmacology consult is the right route. That review would need to happen outside this assistant.\n\nIf one of those works, tell me the drug, dose, and frequency, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
